         <t:abstract>
            <t:p>According to <t:bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/TI8ZP7W5"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Spies1932Evagrius"/><title level="a">Die äthiopische Überlieferung der Abhandlung des Evagrius περὶ τῶν ὸκτὼ λογισμῶν</title><title level="j">Oriens Christianus</title><author><forename>Otto</forename><surname>Spies</surname></author><date>1932</date><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="issue">7</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">203-228</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Spies1932Evagrius</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Spies1932Evagrius</note><t:citedRange>205</t:citedRange></t:bibl>, the Ethiopic version of Evagrius’ treatise only roughly corresponds to the Greek and Syriac versions. 
               It shares with them only the titles and main ideas. The (embedded) colophon states that the text was translated from Arabic during the reign of King <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4428Galawdew">Galāwdewos</t:persName>.
            </t:p>
         </t:abstract>
